    {
      "sourceRef": "index:2",
      "cellIndex": 2,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Problem\n\nCalculate the tension in the string using Lagrange multipliers.\nThe constraint is given by the bead being at $\\vec{r} = \\ell \\hat{\\rho}$, ergo, the function that express this is $f(\\rho) = \\rho - \\ell = 0$.",
      "sourceSha256": "7b67d22cf71876ff0e2a8aebbd2c507c2a7be4f56138fe83ee9070fd5d256429",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\vec{r} = \\ell \\hat{\\rho}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "f(\\rho) = \\rho - \\ell = 0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
